[
{"w":"aphoristic","p":"adj.","m":"Expressed in short, wise sayings.","e":"Greek <i>aphorismos</i> (definition), from <i>aphorizein</i> (to mark off boundaries).","f":"aphoristique, sentencieux","t":"La Rochefoucauld’s maxims are aphoristic."},
{"w":"brusquely","p":"adv.","m":"In an abrupt, rude way.","e":"French <i>brusque</i>, from Italian <i>brusco</i> (sour, harsh).","f":"brusquement, sèchement","t":"Same as « brusquement »."},
{"w":"candidness","p":"n.","m":"Frankness, openness.","e":"Latin <i>candidus</i> (white, pure).","f":"franchise","x":"Faux ami","t":"Candour = franchise, not French candeur (naivety)."},
{"w":"collusion","p":"n.","m":"Secret cooperation to cheat or deceive.","e":"Latin <i>colludere</i> (to play together): <i>com-</i> + <i>ludere</i>.","f":"collusion, connivence","t":"Playing together secretly: « collusion »."},
