{"w":"retract","p":"v.","m":"To withdraw a statement.","e":"Latin <i>retrahere</i> (to draw back).","f":"rétracter, revenir sur","t":"« Se rétracter »."},
{"w":"savvy","p":"adj. / n.","m":"Shrewd and knowledgeable; practical know-how.","e":"Pidgin from Spanish/Portuguese <i>sabe</i> (he knows), Latin <i>sapere</i>.","f":"avisé, futé; savoir-faire","t":"« Savoir »: tech-savvy."},
{"w":"serene","p":"adj.","m":"Calm, peaceful.","e":"Latin <i>serenus</i> (clear, untroubled).","f":"serein","t":"Same as « serein »."},
{"w":"smug","p":"adj.","m":"Excessively pleased with oneself.","e":"Perhaps Low German <i>smuk</i> (neat, trim).","f":"suffisant, content de soi","t":"The smug grin of someone who told you so."},
{"w":"squander","p":"v.","m":"To waste.","e":"Origin unknown (16th c.).","f":"gaspiller, dilapider","t":"Squander an opportunity: « gâcher »."},
