{"w":"taxing","p":"adj.","m":"Physically or mentally demanding.","e":"Latin <i>taxare</i> (to assess, censure).","f":"éprouvant, épuisant","x":"2nd meaning","t":"It takes a tax on your energy."},
{"w":"tout","p":"v.","m":"To promote insistently.","e":"Middle English <i>tuten</i> (to peep, look out). A tout looked out for customers.","f":"vanter, racoler","t":"Touted as the next big thing: « vanté »."},
{"w":"travail","p":"n.","m":"Painful or laborious effort.","e":"Old French <i>travail</i> (suffering), from Latin <i>tripalium</i>, a three-pronged torture device.","f":"labeur, peine","t":"French « travail », in its old sense: hard toil. (Also labour pains.)"},
{"w":"unprecedented","p":"adj.","m":"Never done or known before.","e":"<i>un-</i> + precedent, Latin <i>praecedere</i>.","f":"sans précédent","t":"« Sans précédent »."},
{"w":"unseemly","p":"adj.","m":"Not proper or appropriate.","e":"<i>un-</i> + seemly (fitting), Old Norse <i>sœmr</i>.","f":"inconvenant, malséant","t":"Not seemly: unseemly behaviour."}
